Approved in §128 (Misho's „ყველა კი", 11 Oct) with the field description
in NIGHT_QUESTIONS BF, word for word.

The closed-route check (1697 part 2, §110.1) ran only when an
introduction was requested — after the owner had already approved a plan
whose route could never answer. A propose_task_plan route may now carry
`introduction` (via_phone, to_name, to_phone when a search gave it). The
server runs the same check on that pair before the plan is shown; a
closed route comes back with the §110.1 line and `closed_route` naming
it, so it never reaches the card. The receiver is looked up in the
bridge's own phonebook when no phone was given, as request_introduction
does. Routes without the field behave as before; anything unknown lets
the plan through.

